<title>USA: PCX to trade three new equity options next week.</title>
<headline>PCX to trade three new equity options next week.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pacific Exchange (PCX) said Friday it will begin trading options on shares of Southern Pacific Funding Corp and Willbros Group Inc on June 11.</p>
<p>It also said it will open trading in options on Nationwide Financial Services on June 13.</p>
<p>The following table lists the stocks' ticker symbols and the options' strike prices, expiration months, position limits in number of contracts and lead market maker.  </p>
<p>Ticker     Strikes	Expir	Limits   Lead market maker</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    12-1/2, 15,  Jul, Aug,  7,500    Paul Mandell/</p>
<p>	     17-1/2	 Oct, Jan		Wm. Brandreth</p>
<p>     10, 12-1/2,  Jul, Aug,  4,500    S.Noonan/R. Weiss/</p>
<p>	     15	     Sep, Dec		J. Oppenheimer</p>
<p>    25, 30, 35   Jul, Aug,  7,500    Trent Cutler</p>
<p>				Oct, Jan</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
